# Build context hygiene.
#
# The important entry is `data/`: it holds `secrets.json` (API keys) and the
# local database. Without this, `COPY . .` would bake a developer's keys into
# an image layer, where they stay readable even if a later layer deletes the
# file.

node_modules
.next
out
build
dist
coverage

# Local state and secrets — never in an image.
data
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control and tooling
.git
.gitignore
.github
.codex
.cursor
.gemini
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Docs, tests and specs are not needed to run the server. Keep the image
# small and the attack surface limited to what ships.
docs
tests
eval
*.md
!README.md

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Editor/build cache
next-env.d.ts
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
